  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EASTERN HABITAT JOINT VENTURE CONSERVATION</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project activities will take place in Eastern Habitat Joint Venture (EHJV) Target Areas across the six eastern Canadian provinces: Ontario, Qubec, New Brunswick, Nova Scotia, Prince Edward Island, and Newfoundland &amp; Labrador. Ducks Unlimited Canada&apos;s project activities within the EHJV Target Areas will meet the distinct regional needs of waterfowl by addressing key factors limiting eastern waterfowl populations: duckling survival and settling rates .Delivery of a full suite of conservation actions, including securement, enhancement, management, and stewardship, will realize EHJV waterfowl population goals for six priority breeding species: American Black Duck, Mallard, Wood Duck, Common and Barrow&apos;s Goldeneye and Common Eider. Conservation actions will focus on activities that directly benefit these species and will increase breeding populations of waterfowl with population deficits, such as American Black Ducks.Funds for this award will permanently secure 5,467 acres through acquisition and conservation agreements. Funds under this award will also be used to enhance 630 acres, and to manage 1,132,541 acres.</narrative>
  </description>
